---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro'
import { hospital } from '../data/site'
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Insurance & TPA"
  subtitle="Cashless treatment, empanelled insurers and third-party administrators, and the documents you need."
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <h2>Cashless Treatment at {hospital.name}</h2>
  <p>
    We work with leading health insurers and Third-Party Administrators (TPAs) to offer cashless or reimbursement-based
    treatment. If your insurer is in our network, you may be able to receive treatment without paying the full cost upfront,
    subject to your policy terms, network conditions and the insurer's approval.
  </p>

  <h2>Insurers &amp; TPAs</h2>
  <p>
    The list of empanelled insurers and TPAs is displayed at the hospital reception and is shown below. The list is updated
    from time to time as new tie-ups are added. Please confirm your specific policy and network status with our insurance
    desk or your insurer before admission.
  </p>
  <div id="tpa-list" data-tpa-list>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-400">Loading the current list of empanelled insurers and TPAs…</p>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-4 text-sm">
    If your insurer is not listed, you may still be eligible for treatment on a reimbursement basis. Contact our insurance
    desk for assistance.
  </p>

  <h2>The Cashless Process</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Before admission (planned):</strong> Share your health-card and policy details with the insurance desk at least 48 hours before a planned admission so we can send a pre-authorisation request to your insurer/TPA.</li>
    <li><strong>Emergency admission:</strong> Treatment begins immediately. The insurance desk submits the pre-authorisation request to your insurer/TPA at the earliest, and you may be asked for a deposit pending approval.</li>
    <li><strong>Approval:</strong> The insurer/TPA reviews the request and issues an approval, a modified approval or a rejection. We inform you of the outcome.</li>
    <li><strong>During treatment:</strong> Additional approvals may be sought for extended stay or procedures, as required by your policy.</li>
    <li><strong>At discharge:</strong> The insurer/TPA settles the approved amount directly with the hospital. You pay any non-covered items, deductibles, co-payments or amounts beyond the sanctioned limit.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Documents You Will Need</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Health insurance card and policy number.</li>
    <li>Government photo identity proof (Aadhaar, voter ID, driving licence, passport or similar).</li>
    <li>Doctor's referral or prescription, and previous medical records where available.</li>
    <li>Employer or corporate authorisation letter, where applicable.</li>
    <li>Any insurer-specific forms required at admission.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reimbursement Claims</h2>
  <p>
    Where cashless approval is not available, you may pay for treatment and claim reimbursement from your insurer. We
    provide an itemised bill, discharge summary and relevant reports to support your claim. Please verify your insurer's
    submission deadlines and required documents.
  </p>

  <h2>What Is Usually Not Covered</h2>
  <p>
    Coverages and exclusions vary by policy. Common exclusions include certain waiting periods, pre-existing conditions,
    cosmetic procedures, non-medical consumables and specific room-rent caps. Please refer to your policy wording or ask
    your insurer/TPA for clarification.
  </p>

  <h2>Insurance Desk</h2>
  <p>
    For pre-authorisation, network confirmation or claim assistance, contact the hospital insurance desk:
  </p>
  <p>
    {hospital.name}<br />
    {hospital.address.line1}, {hospital.address.line2}, {hospital.address.city}, {hospital.address.state} — {hospital.address.pincode}<br />
    Email: {hospital.email}<br />
    Phone: {hospital.phones.reception}
  </p>

  <script>
    import { initTpaList } from '../scripts/tpa-list'
    initTpaList()
  </script>
</LegalLayout>
